{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":33509133,"ns":0,"title":"Cutting sequence","extract":"In digital geometry, a cutting sequence is a sequence of symbols whose elements correspond to the individual grid lines crossed (\"cut\") as a curve crosses a square grid.\nSturmian words are a special case of cutting sequences where the curves are straight lines of irrational slope.","description":"Records individual grid lines crossed (\"cut\") as a curve crosses a square grid","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}